Hope you are well.

I will be teaching an ICPSR Summer Workshop, "Sensitivity Analysis: Quantifying the Robustness of Inferences to Alternative Factors or Data <https://web.cvent.com/event/6a962cf4-05e7-45fb-8f6f-eafe8c67ce53/websitePage:17e8f24b-550c-4a09-a091-06ccd6f667d5?session=d13fadd8-f2f4-4912-a587-c7d82a6f3d2c&shareLink=true>," July 8-12, 2024. Hybrid (virtual, FtF in Ann Arbor, MI, with asynchronous access to materials).  See more details below.

Most social scientists need to consider the unobserved conditions that could change an inference. This workshop is about the statistical tools (R,  Stata or the konfound-it app <https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/konfound-project.shinyapps.io/konfound-it/__;!!HXCxUKc!1GBYki9sA_ziaSyV22dh5oY4I6p4JTSIhkasW5dxuY50XaEIxpd9o5-NkZ6jsvB5L3ZNrHR3Xb5s9VhZMIWB$>) to do just that, quantifying the strength of evidence to inform policy, practice, or general social science.

The workshop is a full 20 instruction hours of instruction including opportunities to adapt to specific models such as mediation, moderation, diff in diff, logistic regression, hazard/cox regression, multilevel models, differential attrition from treatment groups, etc.

Go here to register <https://web.cvent.com/event/6a962cf4-05e7-45fb-8f6f-eafe8c67ce53/websitePage:17e8f24b-550c-4a09-a091-06ccd6f667d5?session=d13fadd8-f2f4-4912-a587-c7d82a6f3d2c&shareLink=true>. Group discounts <https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/www.icpsr.umich.edu/web/pages/sumprog/registration.html*:*:text=Discount*20for*20Returning*20ICPSR*20Summer,this*20year&__;I34lJSUlJQ!!HXCxUKc!1GBYki9sA_ziaSyV22dh5oY4I6p4JTSIhkasW5dxuY50XaEIxpd9o5-NkZ6jsvB5L3ZNrHR3Xb5s9dQ8KcrG$> available as well.

